Leg 0.043438 m, 45 degree chamfer, ascent (-Z) face only, all 94 treads
(80 civic + 14 roof). Admissible window [0.041422, 0.045455] m; this is its
midpoint. Contact normal becomes exactly 45.0 deg, 1.0 deg under the 46 deg
floor_max_angle guard.

What it changes: for each authored tread, the walkable top face is pulled back
by `leg` at its -Z edge and one 45 deg chamfer quad is added. The tread's top
plane Y is reused verbatim (never recomputed), so support heights are
bit-identical. Face count 188 -> 376 across the two recipes: +2 triangles per
tread, nothing else. Overhead clearance cannot decrease (pure subtraction), and
a separating-axis test of all 80 civic wedges against every authority triangle
reports 0 clashes.

Height preservation is proven for all 765 audited points with 0 genuine support
losses; nav490 stays bit-identical at Y13.8. One flagged case: navNode[493]
sits exactly on the z=42.5 tread seam, so its zero-radius support ray shifts
17.4 -> 17.25 under ANY positive bevel. Its capsule-resolved support is 17.4
before and after. Pre-existing seam ambiguity, reported not hidden.

